{{also|runup|run-up}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{infl|en|verb|head=to [[run]] [[up]]}}

# {{cricket}} of a [[bowler]], to run, or [[walk]] up to the [[bowling crease]] in order to [[bowl]] a [[ball]]
# {{idiom}} To bring a [[flag]] to the top of it's [[flag pole]]
# {{idiom}}To [[make]] something, usually an item of clothing, very [[quickly]]
#: ''I'll '''run''' you '''up''' a skirt for tomorrow evening.''
# {{idiom}}To [[accumulate]] a [[debt]]
#: ''He '''ran up''' over 5,000 $ in unpaid bills.

